    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "M1 and M2 are classified as Narrow Money, whereas M3 and M4 are classified as Broad Money by the Reserve Bank of India.",
        "M3 is officially recognized by the RBI as the primary measure of total Aggregate Monetary Resources in the economy.",
        "The Money Multiplier is mathematically defined as the inverse of the Reserve Ratio (1 / LRR) or (1 + c) / (c + r).",
        "During a Liquidity Trap, conventional monetary policy tools like lowering interest rates fail to stimulate aggregate demand or investment."
      ],
      "id": "f7dmjuu"
    },
